Give autoloot a chance at locked chests, not just unlocked ones.
Touches: src/server/game/Spells/SpellEffects.cpp, Spell::EffectOpenLock()

Why: chest autoloot (TryAutolootChest/OnPlayerUseGameObject, Living Gear's
module) only ever fired from GameObject::Use()'s GAMEOBJECT_TYPE_CHEST
case -- which turns out to only run for chests with NO lock at all.
Any locked chest (Lockpicking, key, or otherwise) is opened through a
completely different path: right-clicking triggers an implicit "open
lock" spell cast, and a successful Spell::CanOpenLock() check goes
straight to SendLoot() here, in EffectOpenLock(), never touching
GameObject::Use() at all. This was confirmed via a debug pass (temporary
prints, since removed) that showed a real "Solid Chest" (lockId 57)
reaching CanOpenLock and succeeding, while a print on the literal first
line of GameObject::Use() never fired once -- proving the two paths are
genuinely disjoint, not a bug in the CHEST case logic itself. Locked
chests are also the more common real-world case (any chest actually
worth autolooting past trivial early-game ones tends to have a lock), so
this was silently the majority of "why doesn't chest autoloot ever do
anything" reports.

--- a/src/server/game/Spells/SpellEffects.cpp
+++ b/src/server/game/Spells/SpellEffects.cpp
@@ Spell::EffectOpenLock(SpellEffIndex effIndex)
     sScriptMgr->OnPlayerOpenLock(player, lockId);

     if (gameObjTarget)
-        SendLoot(guid, LOOT_SKINNING);
+    {
+        // Living Gear: give autoloot the same shot at a successfully-
+        // unlocked chest that unlocked/no-lock chests already get in
+        // GameObject::Use()'s CHEST case -- fall back to the normal loot
+        // window only if it declines.
+        bool handled = false;
+        sScriptMgr->OnPlayerUseGameObject(player, gameObjTarget, handled);
+        if (!handled)
+            SendLoot(guid, LOOT_SKINNING);
+    }
     else if (itemTarget)
